      "question_text": "What is the derivative of $y = x^{2}(5x - 3)^{3}$ in fully factorised form?",
      "structure": "combine-product-chain",
      "mastery": false,
      "options": [
        {
          "text": "$x(5x - 3)^{2}(25x - 6)$",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "text": "$15x(5x - 3)^{2}$",
          "why": "Differentiated each factor separately and multiplied $2x \\times 3(5x - 3)^{2}(5)$."
        },
        {
          "text": "$x(5x - 3)^{2}(15x - 6)$",
          "why": "Forgot to multiply by the inner derivative of 5 when differentiating $(5x - 3)^{3}$."
        },
        {
          "text": "$x(5x - 3)^{2}(25x + 6)$",
          "why": "Added 6 instead of subtracting 6 when expanding brackets."
        }
      ],
      "solution_text": "$u = x^{2}, \\quad u' = 2x$\n$v = (5x - 3)^{3}, \\quad v' = 15(5x - 3)^{2}$\n$y' = 2x(5x - 3)^{3} + 15x^{2}(5x - 3)^{2}$\n$= x(5x - 3)^{2}[2(5x - 3) + 15x]$\n$= x(5x - 3)^{2}(25x - 6)$"
    },
